  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "She appears beside Fairy Zi Wei after waking, asks to be called sister rather than senior, and worries about wrinkles near her eyes. Fairy Zi Wei greets her as Senior Wan Zi Hong and answers politely that her snow-white face shows no wrinkles. Narration states that most Heavenly Court members come from Central Continent’s ten great ancient sects, but Wan Zi Hong was once a great demon that wreaked havoc in Western Desert and was absorbed into Heavenly Court. She wakes from the immortal graveyard with Zhang Fei Xiong and Gu Liu Ru as Heavenly Court numbers surge against Longevity Heaven.",
      "chapters": [
        1715
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fairy_zi_wei",
        "fac_heavenly_court",
        "fac_ten_great_ancient_sects",
        "reg_western_desert",
        "char_zhang_fei_xiong",
        "char_gu_liu_ru",
        "fac_longevity_heaven"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "She is extremely beautiful and enchanting, with a snow-white, beautiful, and flawless face.",
      "chapters": [
        1715
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "She cultivates wood path, was originally a demonic path Gu Immortal with a deep killing nature, and was recruited by Heavenly Court. Ordered to save Zhang Fei Xiong, she says she likes to kill people, not save them, then charges into his right shoulder wound and scatters into pink petals. Flowers grow into a sea of flowers that replenish his flesh. Her healing clears Nu Er Bao Xiong’s lightning path dao marks, as if her wood path dao marks and Zhang Fei Xiong’s transformation path dao marks do not conflict.",
      "chapters": [
        1718
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "wood-path-healing",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "char_nu_er_bao_xiong"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "She smiles as countless petals drift onto Dong clan’s Red River Wheel and weaken its momentum. Yu Zhu Zi and Ye Qiao Zi defend her while she maintains the moves. Dong clan immortals call her the demoness who scourged Western Desert in history and was recruited by Heavenly Court, and name her one of the most infamous demonesses in history. Fang clan’s Fallen Flower Hall disrupts her killer move; petals roll toward Heavenly Court instead, and the backlash injures her.",
      "chapters": [
        1925
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "petals-against-red-river-wheel",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_dong_clan",
        "house_red_river_wheel",
        "char_yu_zhu_zi",
        "char_ye_qiao_zi",
        "fac_fang_clan",
        "house_fallen_flower_hall"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Under Star Constellation Immortal Venerable’s support of Heavenly Court members, flower petals rain down below Wan Zi Hong among continuous killer moves aimed at Immortal Zombie Giant Sun’s side.",
      "chapters": [
        2199
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "flower-petals-in-formation-war",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_star_constellation_immortal_venerable",
        "char_immortal_zombie_giant_sun"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Leng tells Fang clan that Heavenly Court sent two rank eight Gu Immortals, and that among them Wan Zi Hong was a famous demonic path expert in Western Desert’s history. He notes she is a demonic immortal with no evidence of blood relation to Wan clan.",
      "chapters": [
        2255
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "rank-eight-among-western-desert-foes",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_leng",
        "fac_wan_clan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Narration states that Western Desert’s situation is mostly led by Wan Zi Hong and Zhou Xiong Xin while Star Constellation Immortal Venerable rejects sending help to Western Desert’s righteous path.",
      "chapters": [
        2274
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "western-desert-lead",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_zhou_xiong_xin"
      ]
    }
  ],
